circuit "D flip-flop with reset and enable"

# Chu, Listings 4.1 to 4.4: the D flip-flop, then with an asynchronous
# reset, then with a synchronous enable. At a rising edge of clk, q takes d
# if en is 1 and keeps its value if not; reset clears it at once, clock or
# no clock. 4.4 draws the enable as a mux in front of a plain D flip-flop,
# feeding q back: that mux is what en does here.

clock  clk (hz = 1)
button reset
input  en, d
led    q

q = dff(d, clk, en = en, rst = reset)
